    "title": "Man in Escambia County sentenced for child sexual abuse charge - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ESCAMBIA COUNTY, Fla. ( WKRG ) — A man in Escambia County has been sentenced for inappropriately touching a minor in his custody, according to a release from the Office of State Attorney, First Judicial Circuit of Florida. Tracy Edward Williams will serve 30 years in state prison after entering a guilty plea on one count of Sexual Battery by a Person in Familial Authority. A report that Williams inappropriately touched a child sparked the investigation with the Pensacola Police Department. The abuse allegedly happened for a period of months in 2024. Williams admitted to the abuse when interviewed by law enforcement. The Pensacola Police Department conducted both the investigation and arrest, while Assistant State Attorney, Carrie Gilmer prosecuted. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
